@startuml
' DecisionTrace — Use Case Diagram (Assignment 1 Part I, Section 5.2)
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam actorStyle awesome
left to right direction

actor "Team Member" as TM
actor "Team Lead /\nProject Manager" as TL
actor "New Team Member" as NT
actor "AI Assistant" as AI <<system>>

rectangle "DecisionTrace" {
  usecase "UC01\nImport or record\ndiscussion" as UC01
  usecase "UC02\nExtract candidate\ndecisions & commitments" as UC02
  usecase "UC03\nReview & confirm\nAI suggestions" as UC03
  usecase "UC04\nCreate or revise\na decision" as UC04
  usecase "UC05\nAssign & track\na commitment" as UC05
  usecase "UC06\nCreate & inspect\ndependencies" as UC06
  usecase "UC07\nDetect conflict /\nchange impact" as UC07
  usecase "UC08\nSearch decision history\n& source context" as UC08
}

TM --> UC01
TM --> UC03
TM --> UC05
TM --> UC06
TM --> UC08
TL --> UC04
TL --> UC05
TL --> UC07
NT --> UC08

AI --> UC02

' relationships
UC02 ..> UC01 : reads the stored\ndiscussion
UC03 ..> UC02 : reviews output of
UC07 ..> UC06 : traverses\ndependency graph
UC07 ..> UC03 : flags affected work\nfor human review
UC05 ..> UC03 : may originate from\nconfirmed candidates

note right of UC03
  Human-in-the-loop boundary:
  AI output becomes authoritative
  only after Confirm here.
end note

@enduml
